Chapter: Unicode
  cites Foreword chapter CCE

 Unicode boundary operations -- casefolding, normalization stubs,
 and grapheme/word/line boundary helpers. Operates at the I/O
 boundary where CCE text meets external Unicode expectations.
 Internal compiler operations stay in CCE; this chapter is for
 display, comparison, and interchange.

 Full NFC/NFD/NFKC/NFKD normalization requires the Unicode
 Character Database tables (~1MB). This chapter provides the
 algorithmic framework with ASCII-range fast paths. Full-table
 normalization is a future extension.

 To unicode-to-lower gives a lowercase copy of the text.
 To unicode-to-upper gives an uppercase copy of the text.
 To unicode-casefold gives a casefolded copy for comparison.
 To unicode-word-boundaries gives word-break positions.

 We say:

Section: Case Conversion

  unicode-to-lower : Text -> Text
  unicode-to-lower (s) = uni-case-loop s 0 (text-length s) "" 0

  unicode-to-upper : Text -> Text
  unicode-to-upper (s) = uni-case-loop s 0 (text-length s) "" 1

  unicode-casefold : Text -> Text
  unicode-casefold (s) = unicode-to-lower s

  uni-case-loop : Text, Integer, Integer, Text, Integer -> Text
  uni-case-loop (s) (i) (len) (acc) (to-upper) =
    if i >= len then acc
    else let c = char-code (char-at s i)
    in let u = to-unicode c
    in let converted = if to-upper == 1 then uni-ascii-upper u else uni-ascii-lower u
    in let cce = from-unicode converted
    in uni-case-loop s (i + 1) len (acc & char-to-text (code-to-char cce)) to-upper

  uni-ascii-lower : Integer -> Integer
  uni-ascii-lower (cp) =
    if cp >= 65 then if cp <= 90 then cp + 32 else cp
    else cp

  uni-ascii-upper : Integer -> Integer
  uni-ascii-upper (cp) =
    if cp >= 97 then if cp <= 122 then cp - 32 else cp
    else cp

Section: Case-Insensitive Comparison

  unicode-eq-ci : Text, Text -> Boolean
  unicode-eq-ci (a) (b) = unicode-casefold a == unicode-casefold b

  unicode-compare-ci : Text, Text -> Integer
  unicode-compare-ci (a) (b) = text-compare (unicode-casefold a) (unicode-casefold b)

Section: Character Classification

  uni-is-letter : Integer -> Boolean
  uni-is-letter (cp) =
    if cp >= 65 then if cp <= 90 then True
    else if cp >= 97 then cp <= 122
    else False
    else False

  uni-is-digit : Integer -> Boolean
  uni-is-digit (cp) =
    if cp >= 48 then cp <= 57 else False

  uni-is-whitespace : Integer -> Boolean
  uni-is-whitespace (cp) =
    if cp == 32 then True
    else if cp == 9 then True
    else if cp == 10 then True
    else if cp == 13 then True
    else cp == 12

  uni-is-alphanumeric : Integer -> Boolean
  uni-is-alphanumeric (cp) =
    if uni-is-letter cp then True else uni-is-digit cp

Section: Word Boundaries

  unicode-word-boundaries : Text -> List Integer
  unicode-word-boundaries (s) =
    uni-word-loop s 0 (text-length s) False []

  uni-word-loop : Text, Integer, Integer, Boolean, List Integer -> List Integer
  uni-word-loop (s) (i) (len) (in-word) (acc) =
    if i >= len then if in-word then list-push acc i else acc
    else let cp = to-unicode (char-code (char-at s i))
    in let is-word = uni-is-alphanumeric cp
    in if in-word then
      if is-word then uni-word-loop s (i + 1) len True acc
      else uni-word-loop s (i + 1) len False (list-push acc i)
    else if is-word then uni-word-loop s (i + 1) len True (list-push acc i)
    else uni-word-loop s (i + 1) len False acc

Section: Grapheme Boundaries (ASCII fast path)

  unicode-grapheme-count : Text -> Integer
  unicode-grapheme-count (s) = text-length s

  unicode-grapheme-at : Text, Integer -> Text
  unicode-grapheme-at (s) (i) =
    if i < 0 then ""
    else if i >= text-length s then ""
    else char-to-text (char-at s i)

Section: Normalization Stubs

  unicode-nfc : Text -> Text
  unicode-nfc (s) = s

  unicode-nfd : Text -> Text
  unicode-nfd (s) = s

  unicode-nfkc : Text -> Text
  unicode-nfkc (s) = s

  unicode-nfkd : Text -> Text
  unicode-nfkd (s) = s

